#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:6
msgid "Sealed traits for Polymorphism users cannot extend"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:9
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:10
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:11
msgid ""
"// crate can access the \"sealed\" module and its trait, but projects that\n"
"// depend on it cannot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:18
msgid "//...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:22
msgid "/* methods */"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:30
msgid ""
"Motivation: We want trait-driven code in a crate, but we don't want projects "
"that depend on this crate to be able to implement a trait."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:33
msgid "Why?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:35
msgid ""
"The trait could be considered unstable for downstream-implementations at "
"this point in time."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:38
msgid ""
"Alternatively: Domain is high-risk for naive implementations of a trait "
"(such as cryptography)."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:41
msgid ""
"The mechanism we use to do this is restricting access to a supertrait, "
"preventing downstream users from being able to implement that trait for "
"their types."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:45
msgid "Why not just use enums?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:47
msgid "Enums expose implementation details – \"this works for these types\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:49
msgid "Users need to use variant constructors of an enum to use the API."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:51
msgid ""
"Users can use the enum as a type in their own code, and when the enum "
"changes users need to update their code to match those changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/sealed-traits.md:54
msgid ""
"Enums require branching on variants, whereas sealed traits lets the compile "
"specify monomorphized functions for each type."
msgstr ""
